{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786429251,"nonce":"NZpKnB5BXJXuprH/RorbYeQv1f8=","title":"Every unrecoverable rule in a source collapses into one shared snapshot row","message":"**What is wrong.** `rule_snapshots_content_uniq` is `(org_id, source_id, rule_fingerprint)`, and the fingerprint covers the rule **definition** only — the rule key is not part of it. An `unavailable` capture has an empty expr, zero durations and empty label/annotation maps, so **every unavailable capture in a source hashes identically**.\n\nOne firewalled Prometheus therefore produces ONE shared row for ALL rules, named after whichever alert failed first. The upsert's UNION arm returns that incumbent, so:\n\n- `Capture` hands back a `Snapshot` whose `Key.Name` is somebody else's rule;\n- the `rule.lookup_failed` event payload carries the wrong `rule_name`;\n- `NewVersion` is false for a rule that was never captured;\n- `Latest` filters on `rule_name` and can therefore never find it again.\n\n**Why it matters.** 'What the rule said at that moment' is README's first promise. When rule lookup degrades, the degradation should be honest per rule; instead the history records a confident attribution to the wrong rule, which is worse than recording nothing. It is also self-concealing: `Latest` cannot retrieve the row, so the wrong attribution is hard to notice from inside the product.\n\n**A second, related defect.** The rule key splits when Prometheus becomes reachable: `keyPredicate` is lenient about an empty `rule_file`/`rule_group` **only on the query side**, while stored rows keep `''`. So a query carrying a now-known file and group misses rows captured before it was known — exactly the split its own comment says it prevents. The asymmetry is visible: `generator_url` then `prometheus_api` reports drift, but `prometheus_api` then `generator_url` does not (`Drifted` false, `PreviousFingerprint` empty), so a real rule edit landing in the same fire as the promotion is hidden with it.\n\n**Where.** `internal/rules/domain/snapshot.go`, `internal/rules/repository/snapshots.go` (the upsert and `keyPredicate`), `rule_snapshots_content_uniq`.\n\n**Done when.** An unavailable capture is per rule rather than per source, and the promotion case reports drift symmetrically. Both are pinned today by `TestEveryUnrecoverableRuleInASourceSharesOneRow`, `TestTwoRulesWithIdenticalContentCollapseIntoOneRow` and `TestTheRuleKeySplitsWhenPrometheusBecomesReachable` in `internal/rules/service/`.","files":null}]}